# Engineering

Agent entry point: `AGENTS.md`. Human-readable source of truth: `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Roadmap: `docs/roadmap.md`. Design: `docs/design.md`.

## Workflow

Follow `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`. Do not implement without Issue + branch + eventual PR.

## Layout

- Solution file: **`AgentBridge.slnx` only** (do not create or keep `.sln`)
- Implementation under `src/AgentBridge.*`
- Tests under `tests/AgentBridge.*.Tests` mirroring src 1:1 (Core, Anthropic, OpenAI, Wpf)
- Samples under `samples/` (optional until M5)
- Do not put lasting decisions only in `.dev/` (temporary scratch / review drafts)

## Targets

- Libraries/tests (non-WPF): `net10.0`
- WPF projects: `net10.0-windows`
- Test framework: xUnit

## Analyzers and format

- Nullable enabled; treat warnings as errors
- StyleCop.Analyzers + built-in code analysis via shared `Directory.Build.props`
- Format with `dotnet format` / `.editorconfig`
- Strict XML docs on public API; do not block tests/internal on doc requirements
- **Comments:** XML docs and inline comments must be **Japanese** (type/member identifiers stay English)
- **Test method names:** Natural Japanese, preferably `{Target}_〜すると／したとき〜こと`
  - Example: `FromUser_文字列を指定するとUserロールのテキストメッセージが生成されること`
  - Avoid rigid `前提条件_操作_期待` dumps that do not read as a sentence

## Verification gate

- Prefer `./build.ps1` before merge (restore → format verify → build → test) on **`AgentBridge.slnx`**
- GitHub Actions workflow may exist but **must not be assumed runnable** while Actions are restricted
- Do not mark "CI green on GitHub" as Done while Actions are unavailable

## Branches and issues

- Branch: `type/<issue-number>-<slug>`
- One issue ≈ one PR (M0 may batch foundation work only after an Issue exists)
- Issue types: feat / bug / task / spike (see CONTRIBUTING.md)
